WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.337
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.337 --> 00:00:02.540
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.878
My one word is believe

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:05.620
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.860
all of the major problems of the world.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:11.791
So today's message is
don't be afraid of losses.

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:14.324
Over to you, Robert Kiyosaki.

00:00:14.324 --> 00:00:16.544
(rooster crowing)

00:00:16.544 --> 00:00:18.941
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:18.941 --> 00:00:21.996
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:00:21.996 --> 00:00:25.941
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:29.781
- Well most successful
entrepreneurs have gone bust.

00:00:29.781 --> 00:00:32.548
You know, Henry Ford, an
old-time entrepreneur,

00:00:32.548 --> 00:00:34.815
he went bust five times.

00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:36.420
Okay, look at Steve Jobs.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.253
- [Interviewer] Yep.

00:00:37.253 --> 00:00:38.718
- His own board fired him.

00:00:38.718 --> 00:00:39.859
- [Interviewer] Yep.

00:00:39.859 --> 00:00:42.917
- Bill Gates, was taken
before the Supreme Court

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.729
for monopolistic practices.

00:00:44.729 --> 00:00:45.562
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:48.184
- Even my friend, Donald Trump,
went down a billion dollars.

00:00:48.184 --> 00:00:49.017
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:51.016
- I only went down a million.

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:54.177
So, the average person is
so afraid of those losses

00:00:54.177 --> 00:00:56.307
they never get ahead.

00:00:56.307 --> 00:00:59.657
Because at school, they teach
you if you make a mistake

00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:01.805
or if you fail, you're a failure.

00:01:01.805 --> 00:01:03.659
But that's not real life.

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:07.268
A baby learns to walk by
standing up and falling down,

00:01:07.268 --> 00:01:09.499
standing up and falling down.

00:01:09.499 --> 00:01:12.764
And our school system punishes
you for making mistakes.

00:01:12.764 --> 00:01:17.012
That's why my poor dad, an
academic, was so unsuccessful.

00:01:17.012 --> 00:01:19.337
He was terrified of making mistakes.

00:01:19.337 --> 00:01:20.820
- Most people are so afraid to lose

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.311
that they don't even try.

00:01:22.311 --> 00:01:23.911
We have these big dreams, big ambitions,

00:01:23.911 --> 00:01:25.481
big projects we want to work on.

00:01:25.481 --> 00:01:26.970
And here's the mind twist.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.929
This is why it's so hard.

00:01:28.929 --> 00:01:32.702
It's so fun to think
about where we can go.

00:01:32.702 --> 00:01:34.488
It's so fun to think about

00:01:34.488 --> 00:01:36.272
my channel at a million subscribers.

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:39.460
It's so fun to think
about you on that beach

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:42.170
or you owning that car, you
having that big business,

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.401
you having that big impact.

00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:45.720
It's so amazing, in our heads,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.670
of that life that we want to live.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.670
But doing the work actually is hard.

00:01:51.662 --> 00:01:53.743
And especially at the beginning,

00:01:53.743 --> 00:01:57.942
when you create your first
thing, it's going to suck.

00:01:57.942 --> 00:02:00.122
And you're afraid of how people
are going to react to it.

00:02:00.122 --> 00:02:02.212
The judgment from your
friends, from your parents,

00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:05.043
from the people around you, who look at it

00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:07.013
and say, "That's not very good."

00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:09.500
And as soon as you start making that

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.425
and you get the negativity
and the criticism,

00:02:11.425 --> 00:02:15.335
also from yourself, knowing
that what you made sucked.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.094
It starts to eat away at that dream.

00:02:17.094 --> 00:02:19.692
You start to think that big
dream is not possible anymore.

00:02:19.692 --> 00:02:21.645
And so what ends up
happening to so many people

00:02:21.645 --> 00:02:23.888
is they just stop.

00:02:23.888 --> 00:02:25.555
They just don't do any work.

00:02:25.555 --> 00:02:26.796
They don't take any more action.

00:02:26.796 --> 00:02:27.926
Because they can stay in their head

00:02:27.926 --> 00:02:29.773
and just imagine about the one day

00:02:29.773 --> 00:02:31.296
this thing is going to happen.

00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:34.189
Cause it sets off the endorphins.

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:35.641
It makes you happy.

00:02:35.641 --> 00:02:38.739
But doing the work is painful
and stressful and negative

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:40.711
and, again, every time
you do it, it cracks away

00:02:40.711 --> 00:02:43.353
at you actually thinking
that big dream is possible.

00:02:43.353 --> 00:02:46.034
If you don't do any work, you
can just stay in your head

00:02:46.034 --> 00:02:46.867
and stay happy.

00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:48.125
But what's going to happen?

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:50.155
It's kind of like some of those movies,

00:02:50.155 --> 00:02:51.511
where you know what's going to happen,

00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:53.152
or those puzzles where you
know what the answer is.

00:02:53.152 --> 00:02:55.806
You don't want to do the puzzle anymore.

00:02:55.806 --> 00:02:58.212
The excitement is just in
figuring out the problem.

00:02:58.212 --> 00:03:00.725
And so, it's really exciting
to figure out a problem.

00:03:00.725 --> 00:03:01.794
I know how to solve this problem.

00:03:01.794 --> 00:03:02.926
Here's what Google should do.

00:03:02.926 --> 00:03:04.856
Here's what McDonald's should do.

00:03:04.856 --> 00:03:06.754
Here's what Coca-Cola should do.

00:03:06.754 --> 00:03:08.136
I know how to solve
their business problem.

00:03:08.136 --> 00:03:10.118
It's really fun thinking
through the exercise

00:03:10.118 --> 00:03:11.700
of solving the problem.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.982
But actually doing the work sucks.

00:03:13.982 --> 00:03:15.093
And so people don't do the work.

00:03:15.093 --> 00:03:17.113
They just stay up in their head.

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:19.084
You need to learn to stop that.

00:03:19.084 --> 00:03:20.451
You need to learn to be patient.

00:03:20.451 --> 00:03:22.204
You need to learn to do the work.

00:03:22.204 --> 00:03:23.583
You need to learn to actually go out

00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:26.542
and accomplish the big thing
that you want to accomplish,

00:03:26.542 --> 00:03:28.874
the big thing that you say
is so important to you,

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.223
to get it out of your head

00:03:30.223 --> 00:03:32.334
and start taking the
action to make it happen.

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.104
Because we all have these dreams.

00:03:34.104 --> 00:03:35.335
Everybody has a dream.

00:03:35.335 --> 00:03:36.754
Everybody wants more out of life.

00:03:36.754 --> 00:03:38.725
Everybody wants to have
a greater contribution.

00:03:38.725 --> 00:03:40.655
But most of us are not mapping our actions

00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:42.275
to go achieving those dreams.

00:03:42.275 --> 00:03:43.894
You're not taking the
daily, consistent action

00:03:43.894 --> 00:03:44.968
to make it happen.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:47.042
And so you need to, every single day,

00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:49.491
take some kind of action,
move closer to your goal.

00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:50.670
Expect to suck.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.282
Expect to be criticized by yourself,

00:03:53.282 --> 00:03:55.241
your own hatred of your own work,

00:03:55.241 --> 00:03:56.901
as well as the people around you.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:57.769
That's normal.

00:03:57.769 --> 00:03:58.910
That's to be expected.

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:00.550
Anticipate that.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.550
Because if you go in thinking big dream

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.690
and then your first thing sucks

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.828
and then you get depressed and you quit,

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:07.224
that's not going to help.

00:04:07.224 --> 00:04:08.233
Expect to suck.

00:04:08.233 --> 00:04:09.768
Expect the next one to
suck a little bit less,

00:04:09.768 --> 00:04:11.345
next one to suck a little bit less,

00:04:11.345 --> 00:04:13.077
and taking daily, consistent action

00:04:13.077 --> 00:04:14.543
so you can get out of your head

00:04:14.543 --> 00:04:16.455
and start actually accomplishing things.

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:18.197
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious,

00:04:18.197 --> 00:04:19.787
what was the first thing you did

00:04:19.787 --> 00:04:21.677
to take that big dream that you had

00:04:21.677 --> 00:04:24.547
and actually take some action
on it and implement it?

00:04:24.547 --> 00:04:28.026
What was the first action
item that you took?

00:04:28.026 --> 00:04:29.148
Leave it in the comments below.

00:04:29.148 --> 00:04:30.519
I'm really curious to find out.

00:04:30.519 --> 00:04:32.078
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Eric.

00:04:32.078 --> 00:04:34.380
Eric, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.387
Your One Word.

00:04:35.387 --> 00:04:36.998
I really, really
appreciate the support, man

00:04:36.998 --> 00:04:38.775
and I hope you enjoyed the read.

00:04:38.775 --> 00:04:40.327
So, thank you guys, again, for watching.

00:04:40.327 --> 00:04:41.588
I believe in you!

00:04:41.588 --> 00:04:43.209
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:43.209 --> 00:04:45.537
and whatever your one word is!

00:04:45.537 --> 00:04:47.000
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.519
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:49.519 --> 00:04:52.247
♫ I wake up every mornin'

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:55.830
♫ Entspresso keep me goin'

00:04:58.477 --> 00:05:00.075
- Failure is part of life.

00:05:00.075 --> 00:05:02.299
I mean, the difference for me, though

00:05:02.299 --> 00:05:04.394
is I look at failure as a
stepping stone to success.

00:05:04.394 --> 00:05:05.808
It's a speed bump.

00:05:05.808 --> 00:05:07.448
I know I'm going to fail

00:05:07.448 --> 00:05:09.658
but it's not failure
if you learn something.

00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:12.315
And so, gosh, I've made so many mistakes,

00:05:12.315 --> 00:05:13.616
I've screwed so many things up.

00:05:13.616 --> 00:05:16.669
But every time I do, it just becomes,

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:18.019
it becomes a way for me

00:05:18.019 --> 00:05:19.846
to explain to someone else what it takes.

00:05:19.846 --> 00:05:21.658
You know, it's like,
here's what I've done.

00:05:21.658 --> 00:05:23.789
I think I have the ability
to influence people

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.347
'cause I talk about my failures.

00:05:25.347 --> 00:05:27.608
I talk about all the
things that mess me up.

00:05:27.608 --> 00:05:29.637
But I show people that
I didn't let it stop me

00:05:29.637 --> 00:05:30.866
and you don't need to let it stop you.

00:05:30.866 --> 00:05:32.777
And I think that's really
the secret in that area.

00:05:32.777 --> 00:05:34.478
- And if everything you
touch was successful,

00:05:34.478 --> 00:05:36.559
You probably weren't going
to relate to people as much.

00:05:36.559 --> 00:05:37.496
- No, you're not going to be relate

00:05:37.496 --> 00:05:38.759
and also it's total bullsh--

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:40.235
and everyone know it's bullsh--

00:05:40.235 --> 00:05:41.957
and, also, you'd be bored silly!

00:05:41.957 --> 00:05:42.790
I mean, think about it.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:44.239
If you just said I want
this and it happened,

00:05:44.239 --> 00:05:46.224
I want this and it happened,

00:05:46.224 --> 00:05:49.318
you know, people don't value
what they don't fight for.

00:05:49.318 --> 00:05:50.746
You know, it's like
you see kids sometimes,

00:05:50.746 --> 00:05:52.096
you know, your parents will say,

00:05:52.096 --> 00:05:53.718
"You're not going to value
this if you don't work for it."

00:05:53.718 --> 00:05:56.017
And you're a kid going, "I'll
value it, just give it to me."

00:05:56.017 --> 00:05:56.850
(laughing)

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:58.388
But it's true, you know,

00:05:58.388 --> 00:05:59.996
about the things we've
worked the hardest for,

00:05:59.996 --> 00:06:01.234
we value the most.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:04.346
So, I think, you know,
the purpose of a goal

00:06:04.346 --> 00:06:05.357
is not getting it anyway.

00:06:05.357 --> 00:06:07.725
The purpose of a goal is who you become.

00:06:07.725 --> 00:06:08.925
Who you become is going to make you happy

00:06:08.925 --> 00:06:10.518
or it's going to make you sad.

00:06:10.518 --> 00:06:13.217
So, I'm not looking for
an effortless approach.

00:06:13.217 --> 00:06:14.857
- Sure, sure, sure.
- There's no such thing.

00:06:14.857 --> 00:06:17.107
- You should seek failures.

00:06:17.975 --> 00:06:21.983
See, if you're playing it
safe, you're not going to win.

00:06:21.983 --> 00:06:25.127
If you're playing it safe,
like that old saying,

00:06:25.127 --> 00:06:26.875
you know, you're taught
when you're a little girl,

00:06:26.875 --> 00:06:28.209
better to be safe than sorry.

00:06:28.209 --> 00:06:29.649
Well, that's a bunch of crap.

00:06:29.649 --> 00:06:33.497
It's not better to be safe than sorry.

00:06:33.497 --> 00:06:35.886
It's by trying things that you figure out

00:06:35.886 --> 00:06:38.236
how far you can go.

00:06:38.236 --> 00:06:40.716
You got to get outside the box.

00:06:40.716 --> 00:06:44.695
Like it's reported,
Edison tried 3,000 ways

00:06:44.695 --> 00:06:46.651
before he built the incandescent light.

00:06:46.651 --> 00:06:49.565
He said, he didn't fail 3,000 times.

00:06:49.565 --> 00:06:51.745
He said there was 3,000 different steps

00:06:51.745 --> 00:06:53.828
to building a light bulb.

00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:57.904
Well there's different steps
to get to where you're going.

00:06:57.904 --> 00:07:01.582
And I really do treat winning
and losing exactly the same.

00:07:01.582 --> 00:07:04.255
I do not let it upset me.

00:07:04.255 --> 00:07:05.088
- Do you think that's

00:07:05.088 --> 00:07:08.397
a big part of why you're so successful?

00:07:08.397 --> 00:07:11.877
- Well, it's part of why I enjoy it.

00:07:11.877 --> 00:07:12.736
Yeah, I think it is.

00:07:12.736 --> 00:07:14.654
'Cause I try anything.

00:07:14.654 --> 00:07:16.834
Like, if I'm into an idea,

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:20.167
the idea of losing never enters my mind.

00:07:21.005 --> 00:07:23.588
See, I have worked with giants.

00:07:24.697 --> 00:07:29.506
I had the good fortune of
working with Sir Edmund Hillary.

00:07:29.506 --> 00:07:33.576
He was the first man to
stand on top of the world.

00:07:33.576 --> 00:07:38.086
And I worked with him on
three different occasions.

00:07:38.086 --> 00:07:39.607
And the only difference in Ed Hillary

00:07:39.607 --> 00:07:42.713
and Bob Proctor is his size.

00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:45.516
Now, he's gone now but he was a big man.

00:07:45.516 --> 00:07:46.655
When he shook hands with me,

00:07:46.655 --> 00:07:48.207
his hand wrapped right around mine.

00:07:48.207 --> 00:07:50.707
I felt like a dwarf, you know.

00:07:51.998 --> 00:07:55.144
And talking to him, like
it never entered his mind

00:07:55.144 --> 00:07:57.016
he wouldn't get to the
top of the mountain.

00:07:57.016 --> 00:08:00.433
But he failed in 1951, he failed in 1952.

00:08:01.915 --> 00:08:05.216
It wasn't until 1953 that he
got to the top of the mountain.

00:08:05.216 --> 00:08:09.015
People had died for
centuries trying to do that.

00:08:09.015 --> 00:08:13.186
But he said, "I know if
I can see it in here,

00:08:13.186 --> 00:08:14.513
I could hold it out here."

00:08:14.513 --> 00:08:16.691
Stella Mann wrote that in a book.

00:08:16.691 --> 00:08:19.399
You can see it in your head,
you can hold it in your hand.

00:08:19.399 --> 00:08:20.789
And that's right.

00:08:20.789 --> 00:08:22.519
And if you're not prepared to lose,

00:08:22.519 --> 00:08:26.469
you're never going to win 'cause
you're always playing it safe.

00:08:26.469 --> 00:08:29.250
And there's no reward in that.

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.331
- Yeah, I think failure
is the highway to success.

00:08:31.331 --> 00:08:32.899
And I know that sounds like a platitude

00:08:32.899 --> 00:08:35.322
but society or people teach us, right?

00:08:35.322 --> 00:08:38.428
They say, "Oh, if you fail
and feel uncomfortable,

00:08:38.428 --> 00:08:39.693
you've done something wrong."

00:08:39.693 --> 00:08:41.630
And what I try to do in all of my books

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.607
and my presentations and my tweets

00:08:43.607 --> 00:08:46.607
is you cannot get to the mountaintop

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:51.139
without taking a few missteps.

00:08:51.139 --> 00:08:53.231
And so, a business that wants to win,

00:08:53.231 --> 00:08:55.222
you have to out fail your competition.

00:08:55.222 --> 00:08:57.300
And as human beings, you know,

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.250
failure is not a bad thing.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.083
You know, ask yourself,

00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:01.841
what's the opportunity from the failure?

00:09:01.841 --> 00:09:02.674
And get in the game

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:04.501
because when you get to the
last hour of your last day,

00:09:04.501 --> 00:09:06.362
it will not be the failures you regret.

00:09:06.362 --> 00:09:08.126
It'll be all the risks you didn't take.

